data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_0069eb604cebab19016a68d0fbe5008194916fe713ac149176","logprobs":[],"output_index":2,"sequence_number":517,"text":"FAIL\n\nASSIGNED-MOMENT VERDICTS  \nprimary-job promise: OK  \ninstruction: MATERIAL  \nmantra M-01 (debut): OK  \nmantra M-02 (debut): OK  \nmantra M-06 (debut): OK  \nunassigned passages: OK  \n\n### Voice Gap 1: The first instruction sounds like compliance paperwork\n\n**Our passage:** “**1ST INSTRUCTION: READ WITH CURIOSITY, NOT DREAD; UNTIL YOU REACH YOUR CHOSEN THRESHOLD, EAT AS YOU NORMALLY DO, BEGIN NO NEW RESTRICTION OR COMPENSATION PLAN FOR THIS METHOD, AND KEEP FOLLOWING ANY QUALIFIED CLINICAL INSTRUCTION.**”\n\n**Real passage:** “While you’re reading this book, there is no need to change the way you eat. The time will come when you no longer feel any need or desire for sugar, but until that time comes it’s important that you carry on consuming it as normal. So please keep consuming sugar in the way you usually do, without changing your diet in any way, until I instruct you otherwise.”\n\n**What Carr's voice does here:** Carr gives the direction in ordinary human speech. “There is no need to change” immediately supplies relief, while “please keep consuming sugar in the way you usually do” is unmistakably direct. The reader feels personally released from the pressure to start a diet now.\n\n**Where our voice fails:** The instruction’s semicolon-separated requirements—especially “until you reach your chosen threshold,” “begin no new restriction or compensation plan for this method,” and “keep following any qualified clinical instruction”—sound procedural and contractual. The safety limit is legitimate, but the instruction sentence itself could plausibly appear in a consent form. That register puts the reader under terms and conditions at the precise moment they should feel relieved of another program.\n\n**Initial suspicion (speculative):** commission — the assigned compliance language appears to have been transferred directly into the reader-facing instruction rather than voiced as personal direction.\n\n## Final verdict\n\n**Overall voice-effect assessment:** The chapter generally establishes recognition, autonomy, and the promised end of recurring negotiation without shaming the reader. Its single largest voice-effect gap occurs at the commissioned instruction: “UNTIL YOU REACH YOUR CHOSEN THRESHOLD… BEGIN NO NEW RESTRICTION OR COMPENSATION PLAN… KEEP FOLLOWING ANY QUALIFIED CLINICAL INSTRUCTION” turns a moment meant to create immediate relief into procedural compliance language."}

