ion — the assigned compliance language appears to have been transferred directly into the reader-facing instruction rather than voiced as personal direction.\n\n## Final verdict\n\n**Overall voice-effect assessment:** The chapter generally establishes recognition, autonomy, and the promised end of recurring negotiation without shaming the reader. Its single largest voice-effect gap occurs at the commissioned instruction: “UNTIL YOU REACH YOUR CHOSEN THRESHOLD… BEGIN NO NEW RESTRICTION OR COMPENSATION PLAN… KEEP FOLLOWING ANY QUALIFIED CLINICAL INSTRUCTION” turns a moment meant to create immediate relief into procedural compliance language."},"sequence_number":518}

